  "goodToKnow": "Der Realismus is realism, as an attitude (politischer Realismus) and in art. German literary Realismus (roughly 1848–1890), also called poetischer Realismus, includes Theodor Fontane (Effi Briest), Theodor Storm and Gottfried Keller. In the GDR, der sozialistische Realismus was the official art doctrine. Realistisch means realistic. Like all -ismus nouns, it's masculine. It has no plural."
